      </header>

      <blockquote><p>The last part in the last sentence of the second paragraph of the proof ("where <script type="math/tex">X_B = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B) \times_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)} X</script> and <script type="math/tex">\mathcal{F}_ B</script> is the pullback of <script type="math/tex">\mathcal{F}</script> to <script type="math/tex">X_B</script>.") is redundant, as <script type="math/tex">X_B</script> and <script type="math/tex">\mathcal{F}</script> are already defined in the sentence before.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-4807" class="header-offset"></a>
