    <a id="comment-5458" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/02KH#comment-5458">Comment #5458</a>
        by
        <cite>Du</cite>
        on <time datetime="2020-08-10 16:26:53.348901">August 10, 2020 at 16:26 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>Lemma 02N7 requirs <script type="math/tex">g^\prime</script> to be flat. So this assumption should be added.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-5676" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/02KH#comment-5676">Comment #5676</a>
        by
        <cite><a href="https://math.columbia.edu/~dejong" rel="author">Johan</a></cite>
        
        on <time datetime="2020-11-14 22:11:02.390576">November 14, 2020 at 22:11 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>@#5458: Yes, we need <script type="math/tex">g'</script> to be flat in order to use Lemma <a href="/tag/02N7" data-tag="02N7">20.17.1</a>. But we're saved by the fact that the base change of a flat morphism is flat (Lemma <a href="/tag/01U9" data-tag="01U9">29.26.8</a>) and that <script type="math/tex">g'</script> is the base change of <script type="math/tex">g</script> by <script type="math/tex">f</script>. I have added a remark to the proof <a href="https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/commit/dacf5041c1991704e5c4635a810d00c2c5c2405b">here</a>.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  

  
